# A thread started from the Home composer gets a tab captioned with the thread,
# not with its raw session id — the list has not refreshed at open time, so the
# title has to be resolved again once it lands.
#
# settings: {"window_width":1100,"window_height":760,"open_tabs":[],"active_tab":"","theme":"dark"}

# NOTE: expect_no_text takes a BARE single word, never a quoted string —
# the script parser only strips quotes for expect_text, so a quoted
# argument here is matched WITH its quote characters and can never hit.
# afterhours_gaps.md #47.

expect_text "Home"

# Focus the composer BY NAME. This was `click 646 674` — a literal point four
# pixels inside the field's top edge — and feat/vis-statusmove moved the whole
# composer 26px down (hanabi reserved a status strip at the window's floor that
# Puffin has no equivalent of; layout_system.h). The point then landed on the
# transcript, the typing went nowhere, and six scripts in this directory failed
# on one edit. `click_ui` takes the widget's centre, so it cannot break on
# layout again.
click_ui composer_reply_input
wait_frames 4
type "tab caption check"
wait_frames 4
key ENTER
wait_frames 45

expect_text "tab caption check"
expect_no_text new1
